  "note": "New vehicle (Elite Expansion 2): FC-31.mtb, the Shenyang FC-31 prototype 31001 of 2012 (marking 31001 on the nose, triangular fins, two-piece canopy frame, twin-wheel nose gear, RD-93 class round nozzles) on the F-15C rig (twin-engine single-seater with ailerons, stabilators and twin rudders; the F-22A is built the same way and carries thrust vectoring, which the FC-31 does not have, so it is not the template). Real size by span: 11.5 m (scale 0.68657; the model comes out 17.5 m with the nose probe, real 16.8 m for 31001 and 17.3 m for 31003). The model has one canopy state (frame only, no glass) and closed, painted bay doors: nothing to close. Baked stores cut out (PL-12 and 2 x PL-10 under each wing) and kept in work/elite_expansion_2/fc31/stores; the ventral keel fairing (part 3) is airframe and stays. The model's own gear and wheels; the F-15C cockpit data is not carried over.",
